 "answer_raw": "The current target range for the federal funds rate is **3.75% to 4.00%** [2][4]. As of October 21, 2026, the effective federal funds rate was **3.88%** [2].\n\nAt its most recent meeting in September 2026, the Fed unanimously raised the target range by **25 basis points** to the current 3.75%–4.00% level [6]. This move marked the first rate hike since 2023 [6]. As part of this decision, the Board of Governors also voted to raise the interest rate paid on reserve balances to **3.90%**, effective September 17, 2026 [2].",
